Q1. What is UI?
Answer: UI stands for User Interface. It includes the visual elements of an application, such as buttons, colors, icons, images, and layouts.
Q2. What is UX?
Answer: UX stands for User Experience. It focuses on how easily and effectively users can interact with a product.
Q3. What is the difference between UI and UX?
Answer: UI focuses on the appearance of a product, whereas UX focuses on the overall experience and usability of the product.
Q4. What is Figma?
Answer: Figma is a cloud-based design tool used to create user interfaces, wireframes, prototypes, and interactive designs.
Q5. What is a wireframe?
Answer: A wireframe is a basic visual layout of a website or application. It shows the placement of elements without focusing on detailed colors or styling.
Q6. What is a prototype?
Answer: A prototype is an interactive model of an application that demonstrates how users can navigate between screens and interact with elements.
Q7. What is the difference between a wireframe and a prototype?
Answer: A wireframe shows the structure of a design, while a prototype demonstrates how the design works through interactions.
Q8. What is a user persona?
Answer: A user persona is a fictional representation of a target user based on research, including their goals, needs, behaviors, and challenges.
Q9. Why do we create user personas?
Answer: We create user personas to understand users' needs and design products that are useful, user-friendly, and effective.
Q10. What is usability?
Answer: Usability refers to how easily users can learn, understand, and use an application to achieve their goals.
Q11. What is a user flow?
Answer: A user flow is the sequence of steps a user follows to complete a task in an application.
Q12. What is the purpose of the Figma Prototype feature?
Answer: The Prototype feature connects different screens and adds interactions, such as button clicks and navigation, to simulate application behavior.
2. User Persona Design
Q13. What are the main components of a user persona?
Answer: The main components are name, age, occupation, goals, needs, behaviors, frustrations, and technical skills.
Q14. How do you create a user persona?
Answer: First, I identify the target audience. Then I gather user information, identify common needs and behaviors, and create a persona representing the target users.
Q15. What is the purpose of a user persona?
Answer: Its purpose is to help designers understand their target audience and make better design decisions.
Q16. What is a target audience?
Answer: A target audience is the specific group of people for whom a product or application is designed.
Q17. Give an example of a user persona for an online learning platform.
Answer: My persona is Rahul, a 21-year-old college student who wants affordable courses, video lectures, quizzes, and progress tracking to improve his skills.
Q18. What is the difference between a user persona and a user profile?
Answer: A user persona represents a typical group of target users, whereas a user profile generally describes an individual user's information.
Q19. How does a user persona improve UI/UX design?
Answer: It helps designers understand user expectations, identify problems, prioritize features, and create a user-friendly interface.
3. Online Learning Platform
Q20. What is an online learning platform?
Answer: An online learning platform is an application or website that allows users to learn through online courses, video lectures, quizzes, and other educational resources.
Q21. What are the main features of your online learning platform?
Answer: The main features are course listings, video lectures, quizzes, progress tracking, user profiles, and course search.
Q22. What is the purpose of course listings?
Answer: Course listings help users browse available courses and select courses based on their interests and requirements.
Q23. Why do we include video lectures?
Answer: Video lectures help users understand concepts visually and learn at their own pace.
Q24. What is progress tracking?
Answer: Progress tracking shows how much of a course a user has completed, including completed lessons, quiz scores, and remaining content.
Q25. Why are quizzes important in an online learning platform?
Answer: Quizzes help users test their knowledge, evaluate their understanding, and identify areas that need improvement.
Q26. How would you design the home screen of an online learning platform?
Answer: I would include a navigation bar, search bar, course categories, recommended courses, enrolled courses, and a progress section.
Q27. How can you improve the user experience of an online learning platform?
Answer: I can improve the experience through simple navigation, clear course information, responsive layouts, easy video controls, and visible progress indicators.
4. Social Fitness App
Q28. What is a social fitness app?
Answer: A social fitness app allows users to track their workouts, set fitness goals, connect with friends, and share their fitness achievements.
Q29. What are the main features of your social fitness app?
Answer: The main features are workout tracking, exercise logging, goal setting, friend connections, activity feeds, and progress sharing.
Q30. What is workout tracking?
Answer: Workout tracking records physical activities such as running, walking, weightlifting, and cycling, along with details like duration, distance, or repetitions.
Q31. Why do we include goal setting?
Answer: Goal setting helps users define fitness targets, stay motivated, and monitor their progress toward achieving those targets.
Q32. Why are social features important in a fitness app?
Answer: Social features encourage users through friendly competition, shared achievements, community support, and motivation from friends.
Q33. How can users log their exercises?
Answer: Users can select an exercise, enter details such as duration, sets, repetitions, or weight, and save the workout.
Q34. How would you design the home screen of a social fitness app?
Answer: I would include a workout summary, daily goals, progress charts, friends' activities, a workout button, and a navigation bar.
Q35. What is the importance of a prototype in a fitness app?
Answer: A prototype helps demonstrate navigation between screens, workout logging, goal setting, and social interactions before development.
5. Product Packaging and Poster/Flyer Mockups
Q36. What is product packaging design?
Answer: Product packaging design involves creating the visual appearance and layout of packaging, including colors, logos, product information, and graphics.
Q37. What is a mockup?
Answer: A mockup is a visual representation of how a design will look in a realistic environment or on a physical product.
Q38. Why do we use mockups?
Answer: Mockups help visualize the final design, present ideas professionally, and identify design improvements before production.
Q39. What are the main elements of packaging design?
Answer: The main elements are product name, logo, colors, typography, images, product information, and layout.
Q40. What is the importance of color in packaging design?
Answer: Colors attract customers, communicate the product's identity, create visual appeal, and help differentiate the product from competitors.
Q41. What is a logo?
Answer: A logo is a visual symbol or design that identifies and represents a brand or company.
Q42. What is a poster or flyer mockup?
Answer: A poster or flyer mockup shows how a promotional design would look in a real-world setting, such as on a wall, notice board, or display.
Q43. Why should packaging be shown from different angles?
Answer: Different angles help viewers understand the complete design, including the front, back, sides, and overall appearance of the package.
Q44. What is typography?
Answer: Typography is the style, arrangement, size, and appearance of text used in a design to improve readability and visual appeal.
6. Recipe Finder Application Using Figma
Q45. What is a recipe finder application?
Answer: A recipe finder application helps users discover recipes based on ingredients, food categories, cooking preferences, and dietary restrictions.
Q46. What are the main features of your recipe finder application?
Answer: The main features are recipe search, ingredient filters, categories, recipe details, cooking instructions, favorites, and dietary filters.
Q47. How can users search for recipes?
Answer: Users can enter a recipe name or available ingredients in the search bar and apply filters to find suitable recipes.
Q48. What are dietary restrictions?
Answer: Dietary restrictions are food-related limitations or preferences, such as vegetarian, vegan, gluten-free, or dairy-free diets.
Q49. Why do we include a favorites feature?
Answer: The favorites feature allows users to save recipes they like and access them quickly in the future.
Q50. How would you design the home screen of a recipe finder application?
Answer: I would include a search bar, food categories, popular recipes, ingredient filters, recipe cards, and a favorites section.
7. Additional Important Figma Questions
These questions are also commonly useful for a practical viva.
Q51. What is a frame in Figma?
Answer: A frame is a container used to organize design elements and represent screens, pages, or sections of an interface.
Q52. What are components in Figma?
Answer: Components are reusable design elements, such as buttons, navigation bars, and cards, that maintain consistency across screens.
Q53. What are variants in Figma?
Answer: Variants are different versions of the same component, such as a button in default, hover, active, or disabled states.
Q54. What is Auto Layout?
Answer: Auto Layout automatically adjusts the spacing, alignment, and arrangement of elements when content or dimensions change.
Q55. What are constraints in Figma?
Answer: Constraints define how an element behaves when its parent frame changes size.
Q56. What is responsive design?
Answer: Responsive design ensures that an interface adapts to different screen sizes, such as mobile phones, tablets, and desktops.
Q57. What is the difference between a component and an instance?
Answer: A component is the main reusable element, while an instance is a copy of that component used elsewhere in the design.
Q58. How do you create a clickable button in Figma?
Answer: I select the button, open the Prototype tab, connect it to the destination frame, choose an interaction such as On Click, and select an action such as Navigate To.
Q59. How do you share your Figma design?
Answer: I click the Share button, configure the appropriate access permissions, and share the design link with others.
Q60. What is the difference between UI design and graphic design?
Answer: UI design focuses on interactive digital interfaces, while graphic design focuses on visual communication through elements such as posters, logos, advertisements, and packaging.
